{
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "Term \u2192 postings list with term frequency and positions; analysis pipeline is identical at index and query time",
        "Segments are immutable: refresh flushes near-real-time segments, background merges combine them, deletes are tombstones"
      ],
      "title": "Inverted index"
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "items": [
        "Changes flow from the primary DB via CDC into Kafka, so updates are never missed and can be replayed",
        "Indexers analyze documents and write them to the owning shard; the index is a derived view, rebuildable from the DB"
      ],
      "title": "Indexing path"
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "items": [
        "Document partitioning: coordinator scatters to every shard, each returns local top-K, coordinator merges to global top-K",
        "Stage 1 BM25 on each shard, then business boosts, then an ML re-ranker on the top few hundred; p99 is the slowest shard"
      ],
      "title": "Query path"
    }
  ],
